# nvn/textures: without BC, BC1 / BC2 / BC3 2D textures are stored as ASTC 4x4 (a quarter of RGBA8), transcoded at upload on the GPU (kernel bca) or the CPU; DM_NO_BC_ASTC
#
# Source:    https://github.com/mianmuhammadse/nxnative  branch no-bc, commits 3f0a88d5 ("BC1/BC2/BC3 → ASTC 4x4 block transcoder (C reference) and its test"), 20069e35 ("... as a Metal
#            kernel, byte-identical to the C reference"), 66db65be ("GPUs without BC store BC1/BC2/BC3 as ASTC 4x4 instead of RGBA8"), 30198611 (t_astc_hw, the order fix), 9d90f356 (log)
# Author:    Mian Muhammad (the commits' author)
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE; the fork keeps it). dm/gfx/tex/bc2astc_core.h, bc2astc_body.inc, bc2astc_msl.h, nvn_bc2astc.c / .h,
#            dm/gfx/tex/tests/t_bc2astc.c, dm/gfx/tests/t_bc2astc_gpu.m and t_astc_hw.m are the fork's files, unchanged.
#
# Why: decompressed BC textures take 4 bytes a texel (RGBA8) against BC1's 0.5 / BC3's 1: a game that fits a 6 GB A16 iPhone as BC does not fit decompressed (the fork: Metroid Dread's
#   textures 2.5 GB as BC, 8.3 GB decompressed, 3.4 GB as ASTC). Every Metal 4 iPhone GPU samples ASTC 4x4.
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m, dm/gfx/tex/*: new files; tests):
#   1. bc_astc_tex(): with g_bc_cpu (0510), a BC1-3 texture that is not 3D or multisample is made ASTC_4x4_LDR (ASTC_4x4_sRGB for the sRGB formats) with PixelFormatView usage.
#      DM_NO_BC_ASTC=all (default) | bc1 (BC1 only) | 0 (everything decompressed, the 0510 behaviour). BC4 / BC5 / BC6H / BC7 / 3D stay decompressed.
#   2. pkg_upload_: GPU deswizzle as any texture, then a transcode job per level and layer (kernel bca, the fork's bc2astc_msl.h, one thread per block) that writes the ASTC blocks after the
#      BC blocks in the same staging block, and a buffer→texture copy of them; up_flush runs the jobs between the fill and copy barriers of 0510. CPU path (sparse pools, linear,
#      DM_NO_BC_GPU=0, no GPU deswizzle): nvn_bc2astc after the CPU deswizzle. copy_b2t into an ASTC stand-in transcodes on the CPU (block for block).
#   3. Views: tex_view_to_mtl takes the base's Metal format: a BC1-3 view of an ASTC base names the matching ASTC format (LDR / sRGB as the view), else the decompressed one; the ASTC
#      LDR / sRGB pair joins g_pfv_srgb. Its five callers pass the base they have.
#   4. A new ASTC stand-in made for the GPU (tex_mtl_'s GPU texture path) is zero-filled with constant (0,0,0,0) ASTC blocks (tex_zero_fill_astc; an all-zero ASTC block is invalid).
#   5. gsb_host_ok refuses a BC texture whose host is not BC (an ASTC stand-in of BC2 / BC3 has the same 16-byte blocks but other bytes); sparse_make leaves BC formats out without BC
#      (an ASTC stand-in of BC2 / BC3 has NVN's tile shape and its tiles would go up raw): made whole and uploaded through pkg_upload_.
#   6. The memory line says how many were transcoded on the GPU / CPU; dm/gfx/tex/README.md describes the no-BC path.
# Not ported: the fork's per-game BC3 keep table (dm/games/<id>/bc3_keep_rgba8.tsv, nvn_texkey.h, DM_NO_BC_ASTC_KEEP*): its only table (Metroid Dread) is empty; its Dread benchmark
#   (bench_bc2astc_dread.c: needs game data); its readback refusals 51 / 52 (ours exist: the CPU readback of a packaged stand-in reads its storage, a GPU-written one returns zeros, red 95).
# On a GPU with BC: bc_astc_tex() is 0 (g_bc_cpu 0), tex_view_to_mtl ignores the base, the new gsb_host_ok test is always false for BC hosts, sparse_make's new line is not reached:
#   no behaviour change (t_bc_astc part 4 runs the code with g_bc_cpu 0: BC formats kept, no job queued, no barrier, nothing counted).
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad).
# Tests (M1 Pro, DM_TEST_NO_BC=1): t_bc2astc_gpu (fork) 22/0, 1.8 M blocks byte-identical to the C reference; t_astc_hw (fork) the M1's ASTC decoder against bcdec, every layout within its
#   tolerance; t_bc_astc (new) 937/0 (BC1/BC1A/BC2/BC3 + sRGB, 2D array 30x18x3 with 3 levels, uploaded twice through the GPU and the CPU: byte-identical to nvn_bc2astc; modes; views;
#   copy_b2t; store-back refusal; storage readback; the BC-GPU proof); t_nobc_order C + D (ASTC job + copy + zero fill, 2 barriers; ASTC zero fill alone) 10/0; t_bc_cpu 796/0
#   (with DM_NO_BC_ASTC's 0 mode: decompressed checks). NOT run: dm/gfx/tex/tests t_bc2astc (the fork's astcenc-based quality test; needs ARM's astcenc binary, not installed:
#   make -C dm/gfx/tex/tests run-astcenc ASTCENC=...). NOT run on an A14-A16 device.

