+// ---------- No-BC path, BC1-3 stored as ASTC 4x4 (engine-patches/0511, ported from mianmuhammadse/nxnative no-bc 3f0a88d5 / 20069e35 / 66db65be / 30198611, MIT) ----------
+// Without BC, BC1, BC2 and BC3 2D textures are stored as ASTC 4x4 (LDR, or sRGB for the sRGB formats), which every Metal 4 iPhone GPU samples: each 4x4 BC block is transcoded into one
+// 16-byte ASTC block at upload (bc2astc_body.inc: one algorithm, compiled for the CPU as nvn_bc2astc.c and for the GPU as the kernel bca, byte-identical). 8 bits per texel against
+// RGBA8's 32: a quarter of the memory of the decompressed texture 0510 makes (the fork: Metroid Dread's textures 8.3 GB decompressed, 3.4 GB as ASTC). BC1 and opaque or uniform-alpha
+// BC2 / BC3 blocks are nearly lossless; a BC2 / BC3 block with varying alpha keeps four alpha levels (the fork measured 39.7 dB alpha PSNR on Dread's 88 M BC3 blocks). A compute kernel
